In article <57700021@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu> gjs21046@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu writes:
   I am running NH3.0 on MSDOS and have the following problem: I saved my game
   which I do _not_ want to lose and tried to restart later, but got a message
   'Saved game is out of date'.  Is this a bug, am I doing something wrong..???

   The Wanderer

Not a bug.  The MSDOS version compares the time stamp on the saved game with
the compile date of NetHack itself.  If the save file is older than the
game, you get that error message.

How to solve your problem?  Easy, reset your systems clock, its better that
way as Nethack uses the system time to check for the full moon or to adjust
for special times such as midnight.  You can restore you old game by 
changing the time stamp on your saved game to a more recent date.


